maria-docs: Heads-up — I opened a small PR to change the "pricing tiers" example in the usage-dashboard doc. The table confused a few customers during onboarding demo.
jamal-eng: Thanks — can you paste the old vs new table? want to check the metric names we expect from telemetry.
maria-docs: Old had columns: Tier | Monthly QPS | Per-token cost | Notes. New suggestion: Tier | Included tokens/mo | Overages (per-token) | Typical latency tier. Tried to align with billing API fields.
lee-product: 👍 the latency column helps explain Dedicated vs Hosted expectations. Also flagging that the dashboard screenshot needs to show "model_family" instead of "model_name" to match current telemetry schema.
maria-docs: Good catch — I updated the copy and screenshot. Also added an SDK snippet for estimating monthly spend client-side. Jamal can you sanity-check the JS example?
jamal-eng: Pasting quick check below — using the meter events shape we emit. Please add a short note about sampling and aggregated events.
jamal-eng: ```js
// sample cost estimator (JS)
// assumes `usage` is an array of { model_family, tokens, tier } from our events export
function estimateMonthlyCost(usage, pricingTable) {
  return usage.reduce((sum, evt) => {
    const price = pricingTable[evt.tier]?.overage_per_token || pricingTable.default.overage_per_token;
    const included = pricingTable[evt.tier]?.included_tokens || 0;
    const billable = Math.max(0, evt.tokens - included);
    return sum + billable * price;
  }, 0);
}
```
lee-product: Looks reasonable. Note: pricingTable keys should be the public tier slugs (starter, pro, enterprise). Add that note in the snippet comment.
sam-sre: Small telemetry caveat — when requests hit Reserved pools we tag them with `capacity=dedicated` and cost attribution should map to Dedicated pricing profiles. Suggest adding a blurb in the docs under "Mapping telemetry to pricing".
